Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzle
Author: H. J. Stack
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-06-14
Number: 23
Notes: An X of two stepped bands, 28 rows by 21 columns: one band runs from a single square at the top right (r1c16) down to ONE at the bottom left, the other from ROB (r15) down to FINISH at the bottom right, with PLANT jutting out to the left edge at r18; they cross at EQUAL, URN and BANKER (r21-r23). Squares outside the bands are shown as _. Number printed in the heading ("FUN'S CROSS-WORD PUZZLE No 23"). Credit as printed beside the grid: "This cross-word puzzle is furnished by H. J. Stack of Hartford, Conn." Read by hand from the Milwaukee Sentinel's page (Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_06_14_87.png), solution from Milwaukee_Sentinel_1914_06_21_86.png, by Claude, 2026-11-16.



