2-3. Plural personal pronoun. ~ WE
4-5. Opposite of off. ~ ON
6-7. A conjunction. ~ OR
8-9. Meaning everything. ~ ALL
10-11. A bright color. ~ RED
12-13. Space of time. ~ ERA
14-15. A man's favorite room. ~ DEN
16-17. Possessive masculine pronoun. ~ HIS
18-19. The end. ~ LAST
20-21. An object of praise. ~ HERO
22-23. What school children do. ~ LEARN
24-25. A children's pet. ~ BUNNY
26-27. A machinery term meaning rough edges. ~ BURRS
28-29. A proper name. ~ COREY
30-32. An abbreviation of a boy's name. ~ ROB
33-34. A metal that shines. ~ BRASS
35-36. A summed month. ~ JULY
37-39. An important organ of the body. ~ HEART
40-41. What many men are. ~ BALD
42-43. What farmers do in the spring. ~ PLANT
44-45. The fruit of the cedar. ~ CONE
46-49. What water often becomes. ~ STEAM
50-51. A golfing term. ~ FORE
52-55. A wicked thing to. ~ STAB
56-57. Food for animals. ~ BRAN
58-60. Two and two are. ~ EQUAL
61-62. A kind of vase. ~ URN
63-66. A man who handles money. ~ BANKER
67-68. Keeps you warm in winter. ~ FURS
69-71. Important part of a sailboat. ~ MAST
72-73. A measure of quantity. ~ PINT
74-75. A little animal. ~ TOAD
76-77. To separate into classes. ~ SORT
78-80. It rests you. ~ SLEEP
81-82. A title of respect in addressing a sovereign. ~ SIRE
83-84. A kind of cabbage. ~ KALE
85-87. The first numeral. ~ ONE
88-91. The end. ~ FINISH
1-5. A number. ~ TEN
2-11. Where we live. ~ WORLD
6-15. A small city in western New York. ~ OLEAN
8-19. What a policeman does. ~ ARREST
12-23. A famous inventor. ~ EDISON
16-25. Boy's first name. ~ HARRY
18-27. What the tower of Pisa does. ~ LEANS
20-29. A boy's name. ~ HENRY
22-34. How some animals catch their prey. ~ LURES
24-39. Boilers do sometimes. ~ BURST
26-38. A wild animal in Germany. ~ BOAR
28-52. To build fires in. ~ CRATES
33-47. Determined. ~ BENT
37-46. A possessive pronoun. ~ HAS
48-53. In contact with. ~ AT
49-54. What you may call your mother. ~ MA
55-58. To exist. ~ BE
30-45. To govern. ~ RULE
31-41. Opposite to young. ~ OLD
32-36. Next to. ~ BY
35-51. A girl's name. ~ JANE
40-57. Babies are. ~ BORN
50-64. A boy's name. ~ FRANK
44-60. Something that gives heat. ~ COAL
56-68. What a fire does. ~ BURNS
59-73. A measure of quantity larger than from 72-73. ~ QUART
67-82. Something to beware of. ~ FIRE
72-87. A passage for perspiration. ~ PORE
76-86. Something very wicked. ~ SIN
81-85. In like manner. ~ SO
65-69. A measure of type. ~ EM
66-74. A small animal women fear. ~ RAT
70-78. A wireless call. ~ SOS
71-83. How we express ourselves. ~ TALK
75-88. An awful affliction. ~ DEAF
79-89. A proper name used for a college. ~ ELI
80-90. What we write with. ~ PEN



